=== Experiment 6: FIN vs. RST: Orderly and Abrupt Connection Termination ===

Started Exchange Server (PID 52812).
[server] listening on 127.0.0.1:5000 (fd=3, kq=4)
Exchange Server is listening.[server] accepted fd=5 owner=1 from 127.0.0.1:12772


Part A: orderly connection termination (FIN).
[server] fd=5: connection reset by peer (RST, ECONNRESET)
[server] closing fd=5 owner=1
[server] accepted fd=5 owner=2 from 127.0.0.1:34527
Orderly client: connected from 127.0.0.1:34527
The client will shut down its sending direction.
[server] fd=5: peer closed (FIN, recv==0)
[server] closing fd=5 owner=2
Investigate the TCP traffic and connection state.

Part B: abortive connection termination (RST).
Abrupt client: connected from 127.0.0.1:14618
[server] accepted fd=5 owner=3 from 127.0.0.1:14618
The client will now close abortively.
Investigate the TCP traffic and connection state.

[server] fd=5: connection reset by peer (RST, ECONNRESET)
The Exchange Server will remain running for 15 seconds.
[server] closing fd=5 owner=3

Experiment finished.
Stopping Exchange Server...
